# Cloudflare Pages routing for the SPA.
#
# The client routes with wouter (history API), so a hard refresh on a deep link
# (:lang, /admin, ...) must return the app shell instead of a 404. Cloudflare
# Pages serves a matching static file BEFORE applying these rules, so
# /assets/*, /downloads/*, /favicon.svg, /manifest.webmanifest, /sw.js and
# /robots.txt are still served as real files.
#
# /api/* never reaches Pages: the API Worker owns that path through a Worker
# route on the same hostname (see artifacts/api-server/wrangler.jsonc). That
# single-origin wiring is mandatory — the owner session cookie, the Clerk
# session and the API's same-origin write guard all depend on it.
/*  /index.html  200
